<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lint>
    <issue id="InvalidPackage">
        <ignore path="**/bcpkix-jdk18on-*.jar"/>
    </issue>

    <!--
      Everything below is deliberate. Each entry is something lint is right to flag in
      general but wrong about here, so it is suppressed with the reason rather than
      "fixed" into a regression.
    -->

    <!--
      Moonlight talks plain HTTP to hosts on port 47989 before TLS is negotiated, and pairs
      with self-signed certificates it pins itself. Cleartext cannot be disabled.
    -->
    <issue id="InsecureBaseConfiguration" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      PosterContentProvider must be exported so the Android TV launcher can read box art for
      the recommendation row. It serves only cached box art keyed by PC UUID and app ID.
    -->
    <issue id="ExportedContentProvider" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      Game locks orientation to match the stream resolution. That is the whole point on a
      device that can rotate; letting it rotate mid-stream would resize the surface.
    -->
    <issue id="SourceLockedOrientationActivity" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      targetSdk is deliberately held at 34; see the comment in build.gradle. API 35
      force-enables edge-to-edge and changes insets handling, which collides with Game's
      immersive-mode code.
    -->
    <issue id="OldTargetApi" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      "AV1" is the codec name, not a typo for "AV!".
    -->
    <issue id="Typos">
        <ignore path="src/main/res/values/strings.xml" />
    </issue>

    <!--
      Attributes newer than minSdk are used intentionally for forward compatibility; they are
      simply ignored on older releases. minSdk is 30 and the app targets Android TV boxes that
      sit on 11 and 14.
    -->
    <issue id="UnusedAttribute" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      BatteryState.STATUS_* are compile-time inlined ints from API 31 referenced under an
      existing SDK_INT guard in ControllerHandler. Inlining is safe and intended.
    -->
    <issue id="InlinedApi" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      @RequiresApi would be better than the existing @TargetApi (it propagates the version
      contract to callers instead of just silencing the check), but it lives in
      androidx.annotation, which this module does not depend on. Pulling in an AndroidX
      artifact purely to satisfy a style check is not worth it here.
    -->
    <issue id="UseRequiresApi" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      atv_banner and no_app_image ship at xhdpi only. Generating the missing density variants
      needs the original artwork, which we don't have; Android scales the xhdpi asset.
    -->
    <issue id="IconMissingDensityFolder" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      Gradle version currency is tracked separately from this codebase's lint hygiene.
    -->
    <issue id="AndroidGradlePluginVersion" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      NvHTTP's X509TrustManager is deliberate and is how pairing works. It tries the platform
      default trust manager FIRST and only falls back to comparing against the certificate
      pinned for that specific host when the default rejects it - which is the expected case
      for Sunshine's self-signed cert. It is not a trust-everything manager; making lint happy
      here would mean being unable to pair with any host.
    -->
    <issue id="CustomX509TrustManager">
        <ignore path="src/main/java/com/limelight/nvstream/http/NvHTTP.java" />
    </issue>

    <!--
      Multi-window, split-screen, DeX and freeform were removed deliberately; every activity
      sets resizeableActivity="false" on purpose. NonResizeableActivity argues for the
      behaviour we just deleted.

      DiscouragedApi is the more interesting one and is kept in mind rather than disputed: it
      warns that the opt-out is ignored on large screens from Android 12 and entirely from
      Android 16. That is understood and accepted - the target hardware is TV boxes. If the
      app is ever forced into multi-window anyway, the stream draws under the system bars,
      and the fix is to restore onMultiWindowModeChanged and the isInMultiWindowMode branch
      in Game's hideSystemUi runnable.
    -->
    <issue id="NonResizeableActivity" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="DiscouragedApi">
        <ignore path="src/main/AndroidManifest.xml" />
    </issue>

    <!--
      Reported inside the BouncyCastle jar, not our code. Third-party, nothing to fix here.
    -->
    <issue id="TrustAllX509TrustManager">
        <ignore path="**/bcpkix-jdk18on-*.jar" />
        <ignore path="**/bcprov-jdk18on-*.jar" />
    </issue>
</lint>
